## Context
rules/workflow.md § Cycle (PR 2137): all work moves Imagine → Plan → Execute →
Verify → Celebrate, and cycles nest. Every claw has a skill except Imagine:
Plan to Verify have hunt, gaze and verify-gate; Celebrate has merge, roar and
lair. Imagine has one resident sentence, design/design-note-template.md
and raid's Phase 2, which the 2026-11-01 raid ran inline with only a
blind-spot agent. The author asked for the skill on 2026-11-01, step 1 being
to make room for it in the always-listed skill catalog.

## Children
- 1416 make room (project-scoped skills)
- 1417 the Imagine skill, Blocked-by 1416

## Exit criteria
- [x] Both children closed (1416 moot, 1417 closed in the same event); integration review per roar step 8: nothing to unite with one live child, see Author decisions

## De-risk (2026-11-09)

- One live child. 1416 closed moot, so roar step 8's integration review
  (re-read the union of the children) has nothing to unite. Either 1417
  splits (its De-risk item 2: raid Phase 2 delegation becomes a second
  child after the author's ruling on the per-ticket reimagine) and 1415
  stays a tracker of two, or 1415 closes in the same event as 1417. If the
  1443 note on the bare template shows no skill is needed (1417 De-risk
  item 1), both close together.
- "Both children closed" reads "every open child closed"; 1416 counts as
  closed (moot).
- Do not open the second child before the author's ruling (1417 De-risk
  item 3): a ticket for a decision not taken is a wait ticket.

## Author decisions (2026-11-10)

The author ruled that no Imagine skill is built: design/design-note-template.md
suffices. Raid § Phase 2 writes down current practice (1417 De-risk item 3,
option (d)): the Blind-Spot pass always, the per-ticket reimagine at the
lead's judgment with a stronger worker when it runs. 1417's criterion 3 (the
audit) is accepted; its criteria 1, 2, 4 and 5 are dropped by the author on
the evidence of design/2026-11-09-context-length-strategy.md (written on the
bare template with two advisor reviews) and the 1484/1487/1490 raid, whose
premise check plus Blind-Spot pass corrected two premises. No second child is
opened; 1415 closes in the same event as 1417, as its de-risk note foresees.
